 "method": {
  "module": "pipeline/unseen/history.py",
  "notes": [
   "Flood = water beyond permanent water (dark on ≥ 90 % of NISAR passes): rivers and canals excluded.",
   "RADARSAT-1 (CSA, C-band HH, 1998–2007): one threshold per image from tiles with both river and land (split-based Otsu), after warping onto the NISAR grid and aligning by edges.",
   "NISAR (L-band HH+HV, 2026): our detector, thresholds HH -13.0 / HV -18.0 dB calibrated on clear optical days.",
   "GFM = Copernicus Global Flood Monitoring (Sentinel-1), nearest day ± 3 d. Only from 2015, so not on RADARSAT-1 dates.",
   "C-band misses some water under rice and trees that L-band sees: older years are a lower bound.",
   "Rice paddies are flooded on purpose in season: not all water here is disaster."
  ],
